{
  "chapter_id": "CH010",
  "title": "Spirit, Soul and Body",
  "sections": [
    {
      "section_id": "SEC039",
      "title": "The Three-Part Man",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Man is made of an inside and an outside. The outside is the body, the covering we see. The inside holds two parts: the soul and the spirit. The spirit is directly linked to God; it is the part of us that connects to him without mediation. The soul carries our personality, our mind, our memory. The body is the physical covering that houses both. This is the three-part man: spirit, soul, and body.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA153",
            "SRC004149",
            "SRC004161",
            "SRC004164",
            "SRC004166",
            "SRC004170",
            "SRC004172",
            "SRC004173"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004149",
            "SRC004161",
            "SRC004164",
            "SRC004166",
            "SRC004170",
            "SRC004172",
            "SRC004173"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA153"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000001",
          "provider_handle": "p1"
        },
        {
          "text": "Each spirit has one thing that identifies it and distinguishes it from other spiritual entities: conscience. It is the conscience that marks out the human spirit as what it is.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA155",
            "SRC004198",
            "SRC004199",
            "SRC004202",
            "SRC004205"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004198",
            "SRC004199",
            "SRC004202",
            "SRC004205"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA155"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000002",
          "provider_handle": "p2"
        },
        {
          "text": "The soul becomes the center, the place where information passes between the eternal spirit and the physical body that deals with the external world. I have searched for the right word for this — a database, a communication center, call centers — and have not settled on one term, but the function is clear: the soul is the hub through which what comes from the spirit and what comes from the body meet and are processed.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA156",
            "SRC004215",
            "SRC004221",
            "SRC004251",
            "SRC004257",
            "SRC004276",
            "SRC004278",
            "SRC004217",
            "SRC004218",
            "SRC004245",
            "SRC004250"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004215",
            "SRC004221",
            "SRC004251",
            "SRC004257",
            "SRC004276",
            "SRC004278",
            "SRC004217",
            "SRC004218",
            "SRC004245",
            "SRC004250"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA156"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [
            "UNC016"
          ],
          "paragraph_id": "P000003",
          "provider_handle": "p3"
        },
        {
          "text": "The spirit carries eternal information. It has no age, because it came from God and is complete in him. Unlike the soul and body, which are tied to a lifespan, the spirit knows no age.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA157",
            "SRC004265",
            "SRC004268",
            "SRC004269",
            "SRC004270",
            "SRC004271",
            "SRC004272"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004265",
            "SRC004268",
            "SRC004269",
            "SRC004270",
            "SRC004271",
            "SRC004272"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA157"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000004",
          "provider_handle": "p4"
        },
        {
          "text": "What you do in your body permeates your soul just as quickly. This is why sexual union outside marriage is not merely a physical act: you do not just exchange bodies, you exchange soul. The body and the soul are not separate compartments; what happens in one immediately affects the other.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA158",
            "SRC004292",
            "SRC004293",
            "SRC004297",
            "SRC004298"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004292",
            "SRC004293",
            "SRC004297",
            "SRC004298"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA158"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000005",
          "provider_handle": "p5"
        }
      ],
      "idea_refs": [
        "IDEA153",
        "IDEA155",
        "IDEA156",
        "IDEA157",
        "IDEA158"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
