    {
      "section_id": "SEC040",
      "title": "In Dying You Shall Die",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Having laid out the anatomy of spirit, soul and body, we turn to how that spirit came to its present condition.",
          "kind": "connective",
          "evidence_handles": [],
          "source_refs": [],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000006",
          "provider_handle": "p6"
        },
        {
          "text": "The body was never inherently bad. There was no time when the body itself was the problem. It was sin, not the body, that corrupted man.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA154",
            "SRC004177",
            "SRC004178",
            "SRC004180",
            "SRC004183",
            "SRC004184"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004177",
            "SRC004178",
            "SRC004180",
            "SRC004183",
            "SRC004184"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA154"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000007",
          "provider_handle": "p7"
        },
        {
          "text": "At the Fall, life was cut off from man. He was stopped from even experiencing it, cut off from the tree of life, away from life itself. So his spirit began to die.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA159",
            "SRC004322",
            "SRC004325",
            "SRC004338",
            "SRC004340",
            "SRC004341",
            "SRC004344",
            "SRC004345"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004322",
            "SRC004325",
            "SRC004338",
            "SRC004340",
            "SRC004341",
            "SRC004344",
            "SRC004345"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA159"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000008",
          "provider_handle": "p8"
        },
        {
          "text": "God's warning concerning the tree was not that Adam would die instantly on the day he ate of it. In what concerns death, he said: you will die — you will begin to die. It was the start of a dying process, not an immediate end.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA160",
            "SRC004352",
            "SRC004353",
            "SRC004356",
            "SRC004358",
            "SRC004359",
            "SRC004360",
            "SRC004361"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004352",
            "SRC004353",
            "SRC004356",
            "SRC004358",
            "SRC004359",
            "SRC004360",
            "SRC004361"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA160"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [
            "UNC017"
          ],
          "paragraph_id": "P000009",
          "provider_handle": "p9"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Christ, you begin as a baby, and then you grow to be a son. This is the process John speaks of in John chapter 1, verse 12: as many as received him, he gave them power to become — to become sons of God. It is not an instant status but a process of growth, from spiritual infancy into sonship.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA161",
            "SRC004368",
            "SRC004369",
            "SRC004371",
            "SRC004372",
            "SRC004373",
            "SRC004375",
            "SRC004376"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004368",
            "SRC004369",
            "SRC004371",
            "SRC004372",
            "SRC004373",
            "SRC004375",
            "SRC004376"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA161"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000010",
          "provider_handle": "p10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nobody teaches a child how to lie; nobody teaches man how to connive. It comes out naturally. This is the fallen nature inherited from that cutting-off — corruption that needs no instruction.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA162",
            "SRC004381",
            "SRC004382",
            "SRC004385",
            "SRC004387"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004381",
            "SRC004382",
            "SRC004385",
            "SRC004387"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA162"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000011",
          "provider_handle": "p11"
        }
      ],
