    {
      "section_id": "SEC042",
      "title": "Heart, Soul and Mind",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "In Matthew 22, verse 37, Jesus said: you will love the Lord your God with all your heart, and with all your soul, and with all your mind. He specifically distinguished heart, soul, and mind. But my mind is inside my soul — so why did Jesus distinguish that? This is the key to spiritual breakthrough, the alpha breakthrough.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA166",
            "REF032",
            "SRC004442",
            "SRC004458",
            "SRC004461",
            "SRC004463",
            "SRC004469",
            "SRC004471",
            "SRC004473",
            "SRC004474",
            "SRC004477",
            "SRC004481",
            "SRC004489"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004442",
            "SRC004458",
            "SRC004461",
            "SRC004463",
            "SRC004469",
            "SRC004471",
            "SRC004473",
            "SRC004474",
            "SRC004477",
            "SRC004481",
            "SRC004489"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA166"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [
            "REF032"
          ],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000015",
          "provider_handle": "p15"
        },
        {
          "text": "The love of God is in your heart. With all your heart, with all your soul, and with all your mind — love for God must engage heart, soul, and mind together. It is not merely emotion.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA183",
            "SRC004883",
            "SRC004886",
            "SRC004887"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004883",
            "SRC004886",
            "SRC004887"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA183"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000016",
          "provider_handle": "p16"
        },
        {
          "text": "The first place to develop is your soul. Your spirit is already complete; it is not the spirit that a Christian must develop, since the spirit is already complete in him. The work of growth belongs to the soul.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA187",
            "SRC004924",
            "SRC004927",
            "SRC004930",
            "SRC004931"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
